- 6:40 p.m. The Prime Minister will hold a media availability.

--- RAW SUMMARY RECEIVED ---
PM Carney made his first official visit to Saudi Arabia in 26 years, arriving in Jeddah on July 8, 2026, to meet Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman at the Royal Palace on July 9 [1][5]. During the bilateral meeting, the leaders welcomed the establishment of the **Canada-Saudi Arabia Coordination Council** and signed two specific **memoranda of understanding (MOUs) on energy and artificial intelligence** to deepen cooperation [1][5]. PM Carney also delivered remarks at the **Saudi Arabia-Canada Investment Forum**, confirmed Canada’s intent to participate in the **2030 Riyadh World Expo**, and condemned recent Iranian attacks on Gulf countries while reaffirming support for regional sovereignty [1][9]. The trip concluded with a media availability where Carney defended the visit despite human rights concerns, emphasizing that direct engagement is more effective than condemnation from afar [9].

